          <Pad Id="SUU367W5afgQLbvAPfEEPj" SlotId="N1wCR75Zn1nO63A4lbzDec" Bounds="339,1195" />
          <Pad Id="QFxMEGgaKoAPwvfFnrI8EX" Bounds="85,1230,900,244" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Coordinates: Input Notifications takes positions in texture pixels, origin top left, 1 DIP = 1 pixel (Space DIPTopLeft: 1 unit = 100 DIP).&#xD;&#xA;- ToTexturePixels expects the texture on Stride's unit quad (-0.5 ... 0.5, +Y up) placed by World: the Quad here uses Size Mode Size. Fullscreen: World = Scaling (2, 2, 1), View and Projection unconnected.&#xD;&#xA;- A position off the quad lies outside 0 ... Texture Size: the elements see the pointer leave.&#xD;&#xA;- Keyboard focus: a press inside the texture gives its scene the focus (an Input (String) then gets the keys), a press outside releases it.&#xD;&#xA;- Wheel: horizontal positive = left, as in Qt.&#xD;&#xA;- The Projection comes from the Camera Component, which Stride updates while rendering: after a window resize it is one frame late.&#xD;&#xA;- Another mesh: raycast to UV in the patch and feed positions in texture pixels directly.&#xD;&#xA;- Windows only (Direct3D 11). QtTexture and ToTexturePixels are Experimental.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
